WEBVTT

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:18.330
Pillars have been detected.
Transitioning to Level 1 Alert.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.160
Head to the nearest shelter immediately.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:26.580
I repeat: Pillars have been detected.
Transitioning to Level 1 Alert.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.740
What am I...? I have to fly! I...

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.120
Don't push yourself, Sono.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.580
Guys...

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.950
While on one hand,
it stinks that we couldn't fly with Miko,

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:18.200
it seems God had other
plans for us. Right, guys?!

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:22.450
You've got that right!
This is the chance of a lifetime!

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:29.370
This is basically how we earn our living!
Distracting the enemy is what we do best!

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:35.290
We'll pull the Pillars away. While we're
doing that, get everyone to the shelter.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.910
D-Don't...!

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.490
Look at that. We made our goddess cry.

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:59.120
We're going straight to hell, lads.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.290
In that case, let's make
sure we get a hero's welcome!

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:42.070
Episode 9:
Retaking Tateyama Air Base!

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.740
Hero Cannon, fire!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.080
Shit! There's no end to 'em!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:58.040
Doesn't this thing have a core?!
What's up with this tower?!

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.370
Don't get hit! Our formation's
screwed if anyone goes down!

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:14.830
Let's flush these punks outta here!
It's time to do or die!

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:24.910
Bring it on! Giving up isn't something I do!
I never have and never will!

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:44.450
Remember that movie where
the guys went back in time with guns?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:48.240
Hell yeah, I do. They ran outta ammo and died.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:54.450
I always figured you'd be invincible
with modern weapons and infinite ammo.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:59.330
So much for that idea.
Ancient warriors are legit.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.160
Shit! Shit! Shit!

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:21.790
Not today!

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:27.700
What the...?!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.410
We get him?!

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.490
No! It's still standing!

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.290
Hey! Hang in there!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:44.540
Not good! He needs help!

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.040
Fall back! Keep 'em at bay!

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:49.450
What the hell do they want with us?!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:58.040
I don't know! But if this place used to be
Odin's, maybe they think we came to steal stuff!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.790
Azuzu, are you hurt?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:06.080
D-Don't worry, I'm fine. I was just thinking.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:07.700
About the mural?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:12.990
Right now, focus on staying alive.
You can think once we're safe.

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.490
Claudy, um--

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.040
It's wide open here!

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.790
He needs first aid, and fast!

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.120
Azuzu!

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.870
I'm on it!

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.120
Which way is the exit?!

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.790
Fall back, Claudy! It's our job
to get you back in one piece!

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:50.410
Good luck doing that without my help!
I'll take this side!

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:54.660
Gah, stop being so cool!
I'm falling for you again!

00:06:54.660 --> 00:07:00.700
My wings are named Schwertleite!
If you don't value your life, come and get some!

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:06.080
Damn, this wound! These bandages aren't helping!

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.160
Argh, jeez!

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:12.620
You're scowling again.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.790
What a waste of your pretty face.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.950
Don't talk, all right?! Be quiet!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.450
Everyone, run to the next room!

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:27.120
Huh? You can't run like that!

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:33.450
I'll hold 'em off. In other words,
leave 'em to me while you guys escape.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.540
I was waiting for the right chance to say that!

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:39.080
Sorry to steal your thunder.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:42.790
H-Hold up! We haven't given up yet!

00:07:52.490 --> 00:07:54.080
Just go!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.950
See you in Tateyama.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:04.290
Yeah. In Tateyama.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:21.410
Chasing girls is so old fashioned.
This is the age of gentlemen.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:31.240
Azuzu.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.790
I...

00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:34.660
Get a grip!

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.990
Keep moving forward! Whatever you've
realized, we have to report back!

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:53.910
You've got the key in your head and
we need it! The world's depending on us...

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:58.790
No... The world's depending on you,
Azuzu Komagome!

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:19.740
Sono?

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:30.950
I...

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:38.290
The contractions are so close now,
it's not safe to move the mother.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:42.910
The doctors are in danger too,
but they won't evacuate.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:44.580
But, the Pillars...

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:50.490
Yeah, they're coming.
What could the Pillars possibly want here?

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.910
I imagine they're after the baby.

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:55.120
The baby?

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.490
Yes, the baby.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:02.910
We know Pillars steal life force
from the ground and living beings, but...

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:08.040
There's rumors that they prioritize
young people and children.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.240
And if that's true,
they're coming after the baby.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:15.450
In which case...

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.910
You're giving up and leaving?

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:21.490
Yeah, if the enemy is after the baby...

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.660
Let's give up trying to deliver it here
and help them escape.

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:33.910
Huh?

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.200
Can we race them away by car?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.740
Not while she's giving birth.
And what if the enemy catches up?

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:45.240
Can we set up a delivery room
in the shelter and do it there?

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:50.740
It's hard to lose hope
when you see something like this.

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:59.540
People are out there flying to buy us time.
I won't waste it, 'cuz I'm a fighter too.

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:07.490
If I could fly...

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.620
If I could fight...

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:18.120
Sorry I'm weak! Sorry I'm a coward!
Sorry for just worrying everyone!

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.120
I want to be strong like you!

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.620
Sorry that I'm not strong!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:28.540
I've gotta keep up with the others
and go work. You help evacuate.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:31.990
Sorry for not being able to do anything!

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:35.490
The way you and her fly is exactly the same.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:40.990
So I think if you find out one of those answers,
the other will come to you too.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:45.700
What answer? I'm not anything
like Big Sister at all!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:48.910
I don't know! I don't know! I don't know!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.040
Safe Flight

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:56.040
And if you're so worried that it gets to
be too much, open it up when the time is right.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.950
For some emotional support.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.790
Sono?

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:04.950
"Safe Flight"

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.790
If it ever gets to be too much...

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.120
Big Sister!

00:12:18.330 --> 00:12:23.590
"Don't be a baby, idiot!!"

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:27.540
Sono? What's that inside the charm?

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.410
Sono?

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:41.490
Don't be a baby, idiot!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.200
You're right, Big Sister!

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.450
Don't be a baby, idiot.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.490
I know. Sorry I'm a baby.

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.120
Don't be a baby, idiot.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.790
I know. I know...

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.200
I love you, Big Sister.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:07.740
No! You're in no shape to fly! I won't let you!

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:11.490
Then who'll save the shelter?!
A baby's being born!

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.350
Well...

00:13:12.350 --> 00:13:14.740
If I don't go, I...!

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:18.490
You can't fly like this.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.040
But...!

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:31.910
You're...

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:48.830
Sono, you going out?

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:51.040
Yeah, I'm going.

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:55.870
Analysis complete on Secondary's wall.
It's exposed at 20,000 feet.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.490
Roger that.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.200
Sonoka Watarai, lift off!

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.620
Sigururi.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.490
They recovered again?

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:40.830
Ammo

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.290
Miko!

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:54.620
What the...?!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.790
A miracle?!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.200
Not quite!

00:15:11.830 --> 00:15:14.040
Sono!

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:15.240
Miko!

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:18.200
You're late!

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:22.330
Sorry for being so slow! But...

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:27.450
From now on, I'm the fastest in the sky!

00:15:34.790 --> 00:15:39.290
Sonoka! Watarai has entered the battle!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:40.120
Watarai?

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.290
Yeah?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:42.580
You okay?

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:44.950
I was told not to be a baby.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:47.160
That's Amatsuka for you.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.490
I'll give you the rundown.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:52.700
You guys are fighting in a gigantic Pillar.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:57.790
Even if you destroy its Vandrande,
it'll just regenerate.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:01.450
We beat one that healed before!
There must be a way--

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:06.240
About that... We haven't been
twiddling our thumbs over here.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:10.120
The trick is those gears.
They're like clockwork.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:11.410
Gears?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:17.830
When the Vandrande is hit,
those cogs kick in and the clock goes in reverse.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.950
The enemy goes back in time!

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:21.450
You time thief!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.290
You got this?

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.490
We got it!

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:25.990
What'cha got left?

00:16:25.990 --> 00:16:28.660
One Hero Cannon and some Teeny!

00:16:28.660 --> 00:16:30.080
Only one chance.

00:16:30.080 --> 00:16:32.660
Don't worry! If it's you and me...!

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:37.040
Yeah, we can do it. No, we will!

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.080
Check out that speed!

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:47.690
Now!

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.660
You're mine! Teeny Hero Cannon!

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.120
Woohoo!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:04.700
And the Vandrande?!

00:17:14.410 --> 00:17:16.080
There it is! Miko!

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.450
Right!

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:22.830
Hero Cannon, fire!

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.040
Did it work?!

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:02.620
The Secondary was destroyed!
Zero Tertiary detected!

00:18:02.620 --> 00:18:04.120
You mean...?!

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:10.290
Tateyama secured!

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:14.990
--Woohoo!
--Yippee!

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:22.830
Huh?

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:27.660
We're out!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:28.370
Head count?!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.490
All here! Claudy, pray!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.370
Close, Valhalla!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:44.160
She belongs to Tateyama!

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.910
Sorry. You saved me.

00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:11.040
Say "thank you," dummy.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:16.290
Azuzu, thank you.

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:19.080
Well, thank you too.

00:19:25.450 --> 00:19:27.290
Thank you.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.290
Azu! Claudy!

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:35.410
Let go, idiot!

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:37.790
Vrictory! We secured Tateyama! And you?

00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:42.950
We found something I've gotta report.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:46.370
You flew again?

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.160
Yeah. Guess I'm a Valkyrie too.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.790
"Safe Flight"

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.790
I see.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:57.120
That's a crying baby!

00:19:57.120 --> 00:20:00.910
It was born! The baby was born!

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:10.660
Huh? I...

00:20:25.950 --> 00:20:30.870
Lives are lost on the battlefield,
but lives are born there too.

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.290
In which case...

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:39.370
That gives my wings a reason to fight.
Isn't that right, Odin?

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:49.040
Well, the good news is our base is just fine.
Now we can get a handle on things again.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:51.990
However, there's bad news too.

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.990
Komagome, go ahead.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:59.740
Here's a photo of a mural
we saw on the other side.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:04.120
I think it's the history of Odin...
The history of the gods.

00:21:04.120 --> 00:21:06.990
Is that the giant we fought at Fuji?

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:11.370
That's right. And here beside it...

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:13.450
Odin.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:13.750
Huh?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:14.790
You mean...?

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.040
The old man on the mural...

00:21:17.040 --> 00:21:23.290
...closely resembles Odin
when he first revealed himself to humans.

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:27.660
The question is,
why is Odin fighting at the giant's side?

00:21:27.660 --> 00:21:31.990
But this history of gods concludes
with the end of the world.

00:21:31.990 --> 00:21:34.370
The world's end. In other words...

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:37.940
Ragnarök.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:39.700
Ragnarök?

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:44.830
But Ragnarök has yet to happen.
Aren't we fighting to avoid it?

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.830
We were lied to.

00:21:46.830 --> 00:21:48.040
Huh?

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.410
Ragnarök must've happened long ago.

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.990
The age of Odin...

00:22:02.450 --> 00:22:05.910
The demise of mythology...

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:08.200
That was Ragnarök.

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:13.740
A tale of gods surviving solely in song
from Claudy's Nordic homeland.

00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:17.330
Norse mythology...

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:22.160
Ragnarök is already over.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:28.490
I... I refuse to acknowledge it.

00:22:28.490 --> 00:22:31.540
Ragnarök has yet to come!

00:22:31.540 --> 00:22:35.620
We... have not yet fallen!

00:23:57.370 --> 00:23:58.330
Damn Odin!

00:23:58.330 --> 00:23:59.290
That jerk!

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:00.740
He tricked us!

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.450
"Shades"

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.450
Shades here is one thing!

00:24:02.450 --> 00:24:04.160
"Blondie"

00:24:02.450 --> 00:24:04.160
Blondie here is one thing!

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:05.790
"Shaggy"

00:24:04.160 --> 00:24:05.790
Shaggy here is one thing!

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:08.040
But how dare he trick our girls!

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:08.710
We'll...

00:24:08.710 --> 00:24:09.410
...make him...

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:12.080
Episode 10
The Eve Before
the Battle of Tateyama Bay!

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:10.240
...pay for it!

00:24:10.240 --> 00:24:12.080
And that's a fact!
